\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  1.\cf0  We plough the fields, and scatter
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The good seed on the land
\par But it is fed and watered
\par By God's almighty hand
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj He sends the snow in winter
\par The warmth to swell the grain
\par The breezes and the sunshine
\par And soft refreshing rain
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj All good gifts around us
\par Are sent from heaven above
\par Then thank the Lord, O thank the Lord
\par For all His love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  He only is the Maker
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Of all things near and far;
\par He paints the wayside flower;
\par He lights the evening star;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par The winds and waves obey Him
\par By him the birds are fed;
\par Much more to us, His children
\par He gives our daily bread
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj All good gifts around us
\par Are sent from heaven above
\par Then thank the Lord, O thank the Lord
\par For all His love.
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  We thank Thee then, O Father
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 For all things bright and good;
\par The seed-time and the harvest
\par Our life, our health, our food
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Accept the gifts we offer
\par For all Thy love imparts
\par And, what Thou most desirest,
\par \pard          Our humble, thankful hearts.
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj All good gifts around us
\par Are sent from heaven above
\par Then thank the Lord, O thank the Lord
\par For all His love.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

